  "content": {
    "id": "p89-q69-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "69",
    "prompt": "The HCF of two numbers is 21, and the LCM is 2310. Find the possible two numbers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(21,2310)$, $(42,1155)$, $(105,462)$ or $(210,231)$.",
      "worked": "Write the numbers as $a=21x$ and $b=21y$, where $x$ and $y$ are coprime. Using the product of the HCF and LCM:\n$$\\begin{align*}ab&=21\\times2310\\\\ab&=48510\\\\441xy&=48510\\\\xy&=110\\end{align*}$$\nThe factor pairs of $110$ are $(1,110)$, $(2,55)$, $(5,22)$ and $(10,11)$. Each pair is coprime. Multiplying both entries by $21$ gives:\n$$\\begin{align*}(a,b)&=(21,2310)\\\\(a,b)&=(42,1155)\\\\(a,b)&=(105,462)\\\\(a,b)&=(210,231)\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
